ting CI check runs on KServe builds and fails any build that\n  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (demonstrated by failing a\n  deliberately non-compliant build)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): KServe portion of \"all serving-stack images run correctly on\n  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules\".\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the FIPS regression gating check for KServe builds is\n  delivered and verified in this epic. Bundling rationale: the check shares the\n  same images, builds, and CI configuration surface as the P0 remediation —\n  the epic that converts a surface also authors and verifies enforcement for\n  that surface. It is not independently deferrable: a standalone CI epic would\n  build enforcement for surfaces this epic is still converting, leave this\n  epic's enforcement slice incomplete, and force a second pass over the same\n  build configuration.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47559,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b96ad897b1d1575c","agent_id":"a83cb46151cbe75ab","session_id":"1394d656-32ae-4405-935b-3f7c1b336014","uuid":"52c6566f-4c55-40ad-ab17-b441eb68a45c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:16:22.710Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
