gainst the final builds\n- The rebuilt images pass functional verification of the serving request path\n  on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster\n- A gating CI check runs on these builds and fails any build that\n  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (demonstrated by failing a\n  deliberately non-compliant build)\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- \"Serving data plane\" is scoped here to the images the strategy attributes to\n  the Platform Operator component. If serving runtime images are intended,\n  scope needs adjustment — flagged in the decomposition summary for PM\n  confirmation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Platform Operator and serving data plane portion of \"all\n  serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated\n  crypto modules\".\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the FIPS regression gating check for these builds is\n  delivered and verified in this epic. Bundling rationale: the check shares the\n  same images, builds, and CI configuration surface as the P0 remediation —\n  the epic that converts a surface also authors and verifies enforcement for\n  that surface. It is not independently deferrable: a standalone CI epic would\n  build enforcement for surfaces this epic is still converting, leave this\n  epic's enforcement slice incomplete, and force a second pass over the same\n  build configuration.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48278,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b96ad897b1d1575c","agent_id":"a83cb46151cbe75ab","session_id":"1394d656-32ae-4405-935b-3f7c1b336014","uuid":"e0e8b637-7b27-4cc9-ae75-a0f810fef307","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:16:31.838Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
