{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ca2c9e7a3f5c3f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 remediation of KServe serving images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 remediation of KServe serving images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMakes the KServe component images of the model serving stack compliant for\n34\tFIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters: no non-validated cryptographic modules in the\n35\trequest path, and correct runtime behavior on FIPS-enabled clusters. The epic\n36\talso delivers the CI enforcement slice for KServe builds so that FIPS\n37\tregressions are caught at build time rather than rediscovered at certification.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Audit all KServe component images for cryptographic module usage, producing a\n42\t  per-image module inventory that identifies every non-validated crypto library\n43\t  linked in the request path\n44\t- Replace the non-validated crypto usage with validated cryptographic modules\n45\t  and rebuild the affected images\n46\t- Verify that the rebuilt images behave correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n47\t  clusters (the inference request path works end to end under FIPS-enabled\n48\t  crypto policy)\n49\t- Deliver and verify the FIPS regression gating check for KServe builds: a\n50\t  gating CI check that fails any KServe build that reintroduces non-validated\n51\t  crypto usage\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A module inventory exists for every KServe component image, enumerating the\n56\t  cryptographic modules linked in the request path and flagging non-validated\n57\t  usage\n58\t- No KServe component image links a non-validated cryptographic module in the\n59\t  request path, as verified by the module inventory and the gating check run\n60\t  against the final builds\n61\t- The rebuilt KServe images pass functional verification of the inference\n62\t  request path on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster\n63\t- A gating CI check runs on KServe builds and fails any build that\n64\t  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (demonstrated by failing a\n65\t  deliberately non-compliant build)\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): KServe portion of \"all serving-stack images run correctly on\n70\t  FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules\".\n71\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the FIPS regression gating check for KServe builds is\n72\t  delivered and verified in this epic. Bundling rationale: the check shares the\n73\t  same images, builds, and CI configuration surface as the P0 remediation —\n74\t  the epic that converts a surface also authors and verifies enforcement for\n75\t  that surface. It is not independently deferrable: a standalone CI epic would\n76\t  build enforcement for surfaces this epic is still converting, leave this\n77\t  epic's enforcement slice incomplete, and force a second pass over the same\n78\t  build configuration.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab1609e95ab4f690","agent_id":"a4e1c6bbe89212fca","session_id":"1394d656-32ae-4405-935b-3f7c1b336014","uuid":"dc5cfdb0-7eda-431f-9f92-c2f34f04f090","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:23:22.181Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ca2c9e7a3f5c3f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude