{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d65f490b693397","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 remediation of Platform Operator and serving data plane images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 remediation of Platform Operator and serving data plane images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMakes the Platform Operator component and the serving data plane images it\n34\tships compliant for FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters: no non-validated\n35\tcryptographic modules in the request path, and correct runtime behavior on\n36\tFIPS-enabled clusters. The epic also delivers the CI enforcement slice for\n37\tthese builds so that FIPS regressions are caught at build time rather than\n38\trediscovered at certification.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit the Platform Operator and serving data plane images for cryptographic\n43\t  module usage, producing a per-image module inventory that identifies every\n44\t  non-validated crypto library linked in the request path\n45\t- Replace the non-validated crypto usage with validated cryptographic modules\n46\t  and rebuild the affected images\n47\t- Verify that the rebuilt images behave correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n48\t  clusters (the serving data plane request path works end to end under\n49\t  FIPS-enabled crypto policy)\n50\t- Deliver and verify the FIPS regression gating check for these builds: a\n51\t  gating CI check that fails any Platform Operator or serving data plane build\n52\t  that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A module inventory exists for every Platform Operator and serving data plane\n57\t  image, enumerating the cryptographic modules linked in the request path and\n58\t  flagging non-validated usage\n59\t- No Platform Operator or serving data plane image links a non-validated\n60\t  cryptographic module in the request path, as verified by the module\n61\t  inventory and the gating check run against the final builds\n62\t- The rebuilt images pass functional verification of the serving request path\n63\t  on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster\n64\t- A gating CI check runs on these builds and fails any build that\n65\t  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage (demonstrated by failing a\n66\t  deliberately non-compliant build)\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- \"Serving data plane\" is scoped here to the images the strategy attributes to\n71\t  the Platform Operator component. If serving runtime images are intended,\n72\t  scope needs adjustment — flagged in the decomposition summary for PM\n73\t  confirmation.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): Platform Operator and serving data plane portion of \"all\n78\t  serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated\n79\t  crypto modules\".\n80\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): the FIPS regression gating check for these builds is\n81\t  delivered and verified in this epic. Bundling rationale: the check shares the\n82\t  same images, builds, and CI configuration surface as the P0 remediation —\n83\t  the epic that converts a surface also authors and verifies enforcement for\n84\t  that surface. It is not independently deferrable: a standalone CI epic would\n85\t  build enforcement for surfaces this epic is still converting, leave this\n86\t  epic's enforcement slice incomplete, and force a second pass over the same\n87\t  build configuration.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab1609e95ab4f690","agent_id":"a4e1c6bbe89212fca","session_id":"1394d656-32ae-4405-935b-3f7c1b336014","uuid":"008507bb-628c-4bb6-aeae-fadfeb96bd0d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:23:22.801Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d65f490b693397","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
